# VOXDECK monorepo rules

## Source of truth
- Product behavior lives in `specs/**/*.md` (plain English). Read the relevant spec before coding.
- Update the spec when behavior changes. Do not vibe new product rules.

## Folder law
- `apps/web` — the only runnable product surface
- `packages/` — shared tooling/tokens (`ui`, `tsconfig`, `eslint-config`)
- `domains/` — product logic by domain (`decks`, `narration`, `auth`)
- No giant catch-all `utils/` or `helpers/` folders. Name files for the job they do.
- Do not reintroduce `apps/api` or `apps/studio` (old Deck Agent FastAPI prototype).

## File size & naming
- Prefer small, single-purpose files (`word-timing.ts`, `seed-slides.ts`).
- Split files that mix unrelated concerns.
- Keep hierarchy shallow (avoid deep nesting).

## Safety
- Domain changes need a small test when practical.
- Run `npm run check` (or at least typecheck/tests for touched workspaces) before claiming done.
- Recipient routes (`/d/*`) stay public — never require login.
